  "details": "There doesn’t seem to be any way that would allow me to see the estimated skeletal finger movement instead of the gesture animations, but without disabling the gesture parameters for the avatar. (Like what index controller users get).\n\nIndex users get a toggle that freezes the gesture parameters. Whereas everyone else gets a toggle that freezes the gesture parameters, but also makes the fingers animated. It seems really weird to me that even with input 2.0 index users still get special treatment.\n\nThere really should be two toggles, one that switches between skeletal data and avatar animations. And a separate toggle that freezes/unfreezes the GestureRight and GestureLeft parameters going to the avatar. And this should apply to everyone, even index users, in the off chance that they might want to use the hand animations.",
